    },
    {
      "file": "Words/words.cpp",
      "description": "Then we use a switch case to see if the letter matches a Vowel. For this we are defining each vowel character as a case. The switch will look at the value of the letter passed in, then proceed to the case that matches, if there is a match. Nothing happens if there is not a match.",
      "line": 28,
      "title": "switch-case"
    },
    {
      "file": "Words/words.cpp",
      "description": "We increase the counter by 1.",
      "line": 39,
      "title": "counter increase"
    },
    {
      "file": "Words/words.cpp",
      "description": "Then return the counter at the end of the function.",
      "line": 42,
      "title": "return counter"
    },
